# __APP_NAME__

__APP_DESCRIPTION__

Scaffolded from `@aihu/templates-cf-team` (Aihu __AIHU_VERSION__).

## TL;DR

Cloudflare Workers monorepo with [Aihu](https://github.com/aihu-project/aihu),
managed by [Bun](https://bun.sh) workspaces + [moon](https://moonrepo.dev).
Lint/format via Biome, tests via Vitest, agent-discoverable by default.

## Quickstart

```bash
bun install
bun run dev      # local dev server (apps/web)
bun run build    # production bundle
bun run test     # unit tests
bun run check    # biome check + write
```

## Setup

Copy `apps/web/.env.example.<provider>` to `apps/web/.env` and fill in your
auth provider's credentials. The `.env.example.<provider>` file is
provider-suffixed so the template can ship all three example shapes — only
the chosen provider's file lands in your scaffold; rename it to `.env` to
use it.

<!-- Future: pipeline-rename will drop the .<provider> suffix automatically; v0.2.1. -->

## Project structure

```
.
├── apps/
│   └── web/             # the Cloudflare Workers app (your code)
├── packages/
│   └── shared/          # cross-package types / utils
├── moon.yml             # moon monorepo entry point
├── wrangler.toml        # Cloudflare Workers config
├── biome.json           # lint + format
├── tsconfig.json        # workspace TS config (composite refs)
└── .mcp.json            # agent surface (auto-discovered by MCP-aware tools)
```

`apps/web` is the application. `packages/shared` is reserved for cross-package
types and utilities — start it empty and grow as the app does.

## Agent surface

If you scaffolded with `agentSurface !== 'none'`, this project ships a
`.mcp.json` at the repo root. MCP-aware editors and CLIs (Claude Code,
Cursor, etc.) auto-discover it and can connect to the Aihu agent host
without further configuration.

To opt out later, delete `.mcp.json` and the `apps/web/src/agent/aihu-expose.aihu`
file (if present).

## Deploy

GitHub Actions are wired up:
- `ci.yml` — runs on every push and PR (typecheck, test, build)
- `deploy.yml` — runs on push to `main`, deploys via `wrangler deploy`

Set `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` as repo secrets to
enable the deploy workflow.

